# Ratchet for warning-level findings from `verikt check` on this repository.
#
# These are real findings, not false positives: functions over the 50-line limit in
# code-quality.md, plus advisory anti-patterns. Generated code is excluded via
# check.exclude in verikt.yaml, so everything counted here is hand-written. They do not
# fail the build, because only error severity does — but without a ceiling they accumulate
# unnoticed, and "warnings we live with" quietly becomes the baseline.
#
# The self-check CI job fails if the count rises above this number. Lower it when you pay
# debt down; raising it should be a deliberate, reviewed decision with a reason in the
# commit message.
#
# Measure with a freshly embedded engine — `mise run verify` does this — or the number
# reflects whatever engine your binary happens to carry rather than the one CI builds.
# A figure of 69 recorded earlier was measured against a stale engine and was four short.
